r, x ∉ C → r ∈ Set.Icc s t → u (x,r) = q), (∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t → Integrable (fun x : WSpace n => wDensity u (x,t)) ∧ DifferentiableAt ℝ (wEnergy u) t ∧ deriv (wEnergy u) t = 0) ∧ (∀ a b : ℝ, 0 < a → 0 < b → wEnergy u b = wEnergy u a)\",\"correspondence\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"The parameters n,m and H001 retain precisely the positive finite dimensions. Identify coordinate ℝ^n with Fin n → ℝ and target ℝ^m with EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m); product-space and Euclidean domain norms are equivalent, so open sets, compactness, smoothness and coordinate derivatives agree, and volume on the coordinate product is precisely the specified product Lebesgue measure. A map on positive times admits an arbitrary total extension, and restriction of any such extension recovers the original map. H002 constrains smoothness only on the positive open domain; derivatives there depend only on the germ, so both extension and restriction preserve H002, H004 and pointwise H005. H003 is exactly the fixed unit vector condition, and H006 exactly requires one compact C for each closed positive time slab, with no extra scalar regularity in H005. Conversely the original data produce these hypotheses for every total extension. wDx evaluates the Fréchet derivative on the coordinate unit vector; wT, wLap and the squared Euclidean norms therefore give exactly the prescribed derivatives, componentwise Laplacian and Frobenius density. The conclusion quantifies over every positive real t, asserting Lebesgue integrability, ordinary differentiability and zero derivative of the actual integral, plus equality of energies at every two positive times. Restriction and extension give these conclusions in both directions because derivatives at positive times are local and the density sections and integrals coincide. No condition or assertion at time zero or outside positive times is imposed; the integral has no factor 1/2.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report an actual obstacle using these five direct fields. Countercheck the alleged implication against the complete definitions, quantifiers and inequality directions; a feasible example alone does not determine an extremum. A fact not yet proved or registered in the current draft is an obligation to complete, not by itself a gap. For a mathematical stop, identify the concrete implication and actual mathematical difficulty encountered during normal checking/completion, not merely unfilled inventory or exposition. No fixed time/attempt count or counterexample is required. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP/SUSPECTED_GAP stop for an actual supported mathematical obstruction; INPUT_CONFLICT stops for incompatible inputs. In NL0, use source retrieval and explicit conditional deferral for unavailable primary texts; MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT requires that no complete secondary statement can be obtained. Other stages may report SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE for an actual access obstacle. Ordinary unfinished work is not an obstacle report. No mathematical acceptance is generated.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_assembly_feedback","description":"Read only this author stage's saved candidate, generated proof or full native diagnostics. Positive candidate ID; inclusive line bounds. No other case or arbitrary path is accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["mapping","feedback","proof_source","audit_source","assembly_inputs","mechanical","assembly","inspection","compiler_stdout","compiler_stderr","assembly_stdout","assembly_stderr"]},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","kind","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"0c77323d-c601-414f-837d-319b8e8e14f1","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42650,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":759,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":0},"total_tokens":43409,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_00be3be22c0362a3016ae219a532bc81919e040e2628acb18a":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00be3be22c0362a3016ae219a96a408191bbd9274c89fcb408":{"input_tokens":36,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00be3be22c0362a3016ae219ad47948191880b9c15197022fd":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_00be3be22c0362a3016ae219b0ee008191a4776e755173f96a":{"input_tokens":36,"cached_toke